The canonical HEV rebuild exposed a second issue in the existing seam: archive hashes are not byte-reproducible across identical builds, even though deployment metadata validates. I’m comparing members to determine whether this is archive ordering/timestamps or actual object drift; I’ll normalize only the build output if the evidence supports it, and won’t paper over real compiler nondeterminism.
